Track 1: Spring-Tide Slaps the Gantry
- Story & Context: When ferry-hand Toby Vane pried open the corroded lead cylinder under the Camber Dock slipway, he found a half-dissolved ferric tape reeking of battery acid and wet brine that played three songs simultaneously when run through a battered reel-to-reel deck. The harbor authority attempted to impound the machine for noise violations, but before inspectors could reach the breaker box, six dockside welders matched the cassette’s warbled choir track against a thrashing SP-1200 swing beat. That evening, four hundred shipyard workers stomped their steel-toed boots onto hollow pontoons, roaring out the chorus: "Salt on the strings, swing on the tide, nobody drowns tonight!"
