Track 3: Who Cast Off the Mooring Line?
- Story & Context: According to Solent dock lore, during the gale of November 2019, the master reel of the restored time-capsule tape finally sheared in two inside the control booth, showering orange sparks across the wet mixing console while five hundred harbor dancers stood frozen in ankle-deep sea spray. Rather than surrender to the squall, the choir hurled their megaphone batteries into the churning waves and pounded out the missing 16-beat swing rhythm using rusted mooring shackles against the jetty pilings. The storm cleared by sunrise, but fishermen swear the concrete quay still vibrates with that morning's defiant, throat-shredding shanty: "We don’t need the copper tape, we’ve got the tide in our throats!"
